Pre-release audit (0.502..HEAD -> 0.503). Exactly one feat!: commit since the last tag (0.502): d326f95 "feat!: extract the Raider/Raid layer into langertha-raider" (ADR 0026). It is documented in Changes:379-391 ("Raider extracted to the sibling distribution langertha-raider...") but, unlike the other breaking bullet in this release (Changes:278-283, OpenAIResponses client-executed built-ins, which opens with "Incompatible change:"), the Raider-extraction bullet carries no BREAKING / "Incompatible change:" marker despite removing an entire public subsystem (Langertha::Raider, Langertha::Raid, Raider::Result, the raider_mcp self-tools, etc.) from core. Changes is published verbatim as GitHub release notes (GitHub::CreateRelease, notes_from=ChangeLog per the getty-perl-release-author-getty skill), so a consumer skimming for breaking changes can miss this one. Recommend prefixing the bullet with "Incompatible change:" (or an equivalent marker) for consistency with the other flagged breaking bullet. Editing-only, langertha-pod-writer lane.

